    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d94-a1">

                <pb facs="0215" n="121" sameAs="frus:frus1896/pg121"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure in No. 640.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Wetter to Mr.
                            Uhl.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Consulate of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Tamatave</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1896-02-20"><hi rendition="#italic">February 20,
                        1896</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 133.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to transmit herewith some
                    further correspondence pertinent to the inclosures contained in my No. 130 of
                    February 18, 1896, inclosure No. 1 being a copy of Resident Ferraud’s letter No.
                    3 of February 20, 1896; inclosure No. 2 being my reply thereto, reiterating
                    demand for a “status quo” on this question pending instructions; inclosure No. 3
                    being my letter to Resident-General Laroche in re this matter of jurisdiction,
                    reiterating same demand made to Mr. Ferraud.</p>
                <p>I understand Acting British Consul McMillan made in person a similar protest to
                    what I made in writing.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Edw. Telfair Wetter</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">United States Consul.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
